###############################################################################
# Q11 -- Computational resources
###############################################################################

# PFT runs use one NVIDIA A100 80GB GPU (batch 16, 200 epochs); the
# MACE-MP-0 PFT took 30 A100 hours (about 1% of its pretraining). The
# Nequix OAM base model took about 250 A100 hours (OMat24) plus 40 A100
# hours (OAM fine-tuning). Stochastic HVP training is about 30x faster and
# uses 90x less memory than full-Hessian training for a 90K-parameter test
# model (App. A.1).

###############################################################################
# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - Phonon-property MAEs (Table 1), third-order force-constant MAEs in meV/A3 (Table 2), kappa_SRME (Table 3) and elastic-modulus errors (Table A.3) are property errors with no metric type in the schema. Matbench Discovery MAE is in eV/atom (converted).
# - Nequix is a new registry method (method paper not in the corpus). The 90K-parameter full-Hessian test models of App. A.1 are not encoded.
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: datacite).
# - Evaluation roles and data, base models, inference timings with their system sizes, and the source location of each value are recorded in the encoding input (artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/koker2026.yaml) until the schema has terms for them.

